#Chek list for compliance - For Rover and drone
**notes: the character (__) is meant to be used as a checklist/checkbox**
__ All requirements on Appendix 3 are met:
__ Communications requirements all met: communications with the rover shall be designed for use of legally legally available frequencies and power levels
__ Max. distance between rover and antenna: ≤ 100 meters
__ Standard communication: WiFi 2.4Ghz / 5GHz
Accepted frequencies:
__ 144 - 146 MHz
__ 430 - 440 MHz
__ 1240 - 1300 MHz
__ 5650 - 5850 MHz

__ At least one team member has an amateur radio license (CEPT class T/R 61-01)
__ If using 2.4 GHz Band (2412 - 2472 MHz)
Only Wi-fi communication standard is accepted (IEEE 802.11)
Accepted channels:
 1-13 (centre frequency 2412 MHz = 2472 MHz). 
Wifi channel 1 spans from 2400 MHz and the last Wi-Fi channel (14 - not accepted at the ERC) is still 2495 MHz. That range is protected and cannot be used by any other communication devices than the WiFi 802.11.
Up to 100mW EIRP
Accepted standards: IEEE 802.11 b/g/n
Rover can use only one 20 MHz channel
SSID should be set to “ERC_TeamName”.

__ If using 5 GHz Low Band (5150  - 5725 MHz)
Only two 40 MHz channels for wireless Access Systems: 
Wi-fi and AirMax only
Up to 1 W EIRP power
Wider channel allocation (80MHz) only after requested permission from organizers.
SSID should be set to “ERC_TeamName_(A/B)
At least one or two allocated channels will not be a DFS channel (if possible to set by the Team on their equipment).

__ If using 5 GHZ High Band (5725 - 5875 MHz)
Can use two 30 MHz channels for any communication system - FPV, etc.
If using ISM (Industrial, Scientific, Medical ) Bands: 
Team must designate which rule is in compliance with European regulations (https://www.thethingsnetwork.org/docs/lorawan/regional-limitations-of-rf-use/ )
Voice communication using a 500 mW PMR licensed transceiver is allowed on following channels frequencies (MHz): 
▪ 446,00625
▪ 446,01875
▪ 446,03125
▪ 446,04375
▪ 446,05625
▪ 446,06875
▪ 446,08125 - reserved for the organizer
▪ 446,09375 - reserved for the organizer

__ If mobile networks are used: communications via mobile networks (4G, 5G, LTE, etc)
Other communications: must be allowed/legal and documented and agreed by the organizer.
Before the competition: Team should bring 2x filled Radio frequency check cards (appendix 4) for every task (do they need to be printed in advance? Can they be printed at the competition?)
Deliver correct RF form at least 2 weeks before participating to receive points.
